From: RK3128 reference #416 <reference@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] lima: default to 4 PLBs per context

The PLB ring index advances per job, and the GP of job k waits for the
PP of job k - LIMA_CTX_NUM_PLB. With the default of 2 and an app that
renders 4-5 jobs a frame, the next frame's GP can never overlap this
frame's PP. 4 (the existing maximum) lets frames pipeline: the
RK3128 reference Demo on a Mali-400 at 297 MHz dropped 30 frames a loop
with 2 and 14 with 4 (before its shader patches; none with them).
---
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/lima/lima_context.h
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/lima/lima_context.h
@@ -240,9 +240,14 @@
    unsigned min_index;
    unsigned max_index;
 
+   /* plb_index turns per job, not per frame, and the GP of job k writes plb[i] and gp_tile_heap[i], which the PP of
+    * job k - num_plb reads (implicit sync in the kernel): with 2 and an app of 4-5 jobs a frame (offscreen passes),
+    * the on-screen GP of frame N+1 waits for the on-screen PP of frame N, so frames never overlap. 4 lets them
+    * (RK3128 reference #416, its Demo on a Mali-400 at 297 MHz: 30 late frames a loop with 2, 14 with 4).
+    * LIMA_CTX_NUM_PLB still picks 1-4. */
    #define LIMA_CTX_PLB_MIN_NUM  1
    #define LIMA_CTX_PLB_MAX_NUM  4
-   #define LIMA_CTX_PLB_DEF_NUM  2
+   #define LIMA_CTX_PLB_DEF_NUM  4
    #define LIMA_CTX_PLB_BLK_SIZE 512
    unsigned plb_size;
    unsigned plb_gp_size;
